/*
 * Declares the MemoryInterpret module, responsible for reducing memory-related
 * generator values during compile-time interpretation.
 *
 * This includes address-taking, aliasing, referencing, dereferencing, and
 * memory-manipulation constructs. Most memory operators cannot be folded at
 * compile time, but their operands may still be reduced.
 *
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::interpret::memory
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/interpret/memory.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-16
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
